Some excellent suggestions here, thanks.

Obviously mind flayers should be given enough credit to pull the bag
off your head (unless it's sufficiently slippery.)
Of course, then it raises the question "why can't they pull off your
helmet as well?"...and maybe they should. (Or, maybe just the master
mind flayers.)

I tend to think that the charisma stat is indicative of much more than
what form your head comes in.

In the event of a worn bag of holding being cursed... well, I'm not
really sure what "heavy-headed" would entail. The worst possible
scenario is a blessed bag of holding with weight 100 becoming cursed,
sending it to 800 - which isn't pretty. I suppose I might as well make
wearing a bag with weight >200 confer fumbling (i.e you have trouble
keeping balance) and also making it so that when the 800 bag is
uncursed (i.e drops to 400) it falls off your head of its own accord.

> Water-related rust should only prevented if the bag is an oilskin sack.
 > I'm not sure about other kinds of corrosion.

My logic behind this is based on the following example: if you fall
into a pool with a bag, only some of the bag's contents take water
damage.



